WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.200
Here is the payment test scenario.
A one-hundred-dollar Canadian

00:00:03.253 --> 00:00:06.240
transfer is accepted,
but the response times out.

00:00:06.400 --> 00:00:09.280
The customer retries.
We deliberately inject

00:00:09.320 --> 00:00:13.200
a duplicate-posting defect to see
whether our tests catch a second debit.

00:00:13.400 --> 00:00:16.160
The correct result is one transfer,

00:00:16.200 --> 00:00:19.600
one balanced journal and one
customer-visible outcome.

00:00:19.792 --> 00:00:23.120
This is a testing scenario,
not a reported banking incident.

00:00:23.307 --> 00:00:26.560
It gives the modernization effort
a concrete behavior to prove.
